1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,221
EPISODE 2

4
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:16,558
-[gasps]

5
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,190
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

6
00:01:08,527 --> 00:01:10,112
[in Korean] Hey…

7
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:12,322
You all right?

8
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,324
-[screams, pants]
-[groans]

9
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,952
-[in English] What are you doing?
-Man… [groans]

10
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,622
[in Korean] Come on!

11
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,542
[in English] Who are you?

12
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:26,420
You ruined my farm, didn't you?

13
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:30,424
[in Korean] Wait, what in the…
What's she even saying?

14
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,426
Hey, just wait.

15
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:34,261
Okay.

16
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,974
This land is my property.
You fainted right in front of me,

17
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:41,059
and that's why I had
to lay you down for a bit.

18
00:01:41,143 --> 00:01:43,353
I mean, why are you acting like this? Huh?

19
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,564
-[in English] What?
-Oh.

20
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,025
THIS LAND IS MY PROPERTY.

21
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,735
YOU FAINTED,
AND I LAID YOU DOWN FOR A BIT.

22
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:50,986
WHY ARE YOU ACTING LIKE THIS?

23
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:57,409
You're a scam artist.
So stealing from my farm wasn't enough?

24
00:01:57,993 --> 00:01:58,994
[in Korean] Hey, what…

25
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:00,579
Man, what is she saying?

26
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:02,622
What, "scam you"? "Steal from you"?

27
00:02:02,706 --> 00:02:05,250
[in English] Are you kidding me?
Look at your destruction.

28
00:02:05,334 --> 00:02:07,002
And you ate all my strawberries.

29
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:08,086
[in Korean] What…

30
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:11,173
Seriously. Man, this is frustrating.

31
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:13,592
Look, you got it all wrong.
These strawberries were…

32
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:16,470
[in English] You owe me an explanation.

33
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:26,313
[child cheering] <i>Thank you.</i>

34
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,860
[in Korean] What'd I tell you, huh?
I… Right.

35
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:33,862
Here.

36
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:36,073
I told you it wasn't me.

37
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:37,783
I TOLD YOU IT WASN'T ME.

38
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:43,580
[in English] Well… Okay…
Tell me what you're doing here then.

39
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,415
[in Korean] I own this property.

40
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,505
What would my farm be doing here

41
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:54,007
if you were the owner, huh?
That doesn't make sense does it?

42
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,137
[in Korean] Geez, ugh.

43
00:03:00,472 --> 00:03:01,682
Here, look at this.

44
00:03:03,642 --> 00:03:06,144
Read this, okay? Look.

45
00:03:08,814 --> 00:03:09,815
I mean…

46
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,484
Technically, you're the thief here.

47
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:16,196
You're growing crops on someone else's
property without permission.

48
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,582
[in English] Huh?

49
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:31,294
[in Korean] Wait…

50
00:03:32,254 --> 00:03:34,297
Why is there a…

51
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:36,091
[officer, in English] See this tiny spot?

52
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:38,718
You don't own this lot here.

53
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:45,267
This specific plot
is owned by Ms. Shirahama Karin. Hmm?

54
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:50,522
-Huh? M-Ms. Karin? Shirahama Karin?
-[officer] Mm-hmm.

55
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:51,773
[Yubin] Ms. Karin…

56
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:55,235
In other words, it's my property.

57
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:59,948
"My… My property"?

58
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:06,538
You walked onto my private property
and you single-handedly ruined everything.

59
00:04:10,459 --> 00:04:12,335
Ah… [sighs]

60
00:04:12,419 --> 00:04:13,670
[in Korean] No, that's…

61
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:17,924
I mean, it's not like I did it on purpose.

62
00:04:20,302 --> 00:04:23,597
I mean, you can't go calling me a thief
over eating one lousy strawberry.

63
00:04:25,474 --> 00:04:27,642
YOU CAN'T GO CALLING ME A THIEF

64
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:29,394
OVER EATING
ONE LOUSY STRAWBERRY

65
00:04:31,563 --> 00:04:33,774
"One lousy strawberry"?

66
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,529
That is the rudest thing I've ever heard.

67
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,281
[in Korean] Hey, wait.

68
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:48,121
[in English] Excuse me.
We're closed. It's after 5 o'clock.

69
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:50,957
[Yubin] Uh…

70
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:54,586
[in Korean] Seriously, I can't understand
a thing they're saying.

71
00:04:55,754 --> 00:04:57,047
Wait a minute.

72
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,590
Hey, I said wait.

73
00:04:58,673 --> 00:04:59,925
Wait.

74
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:07,516
I'll make it all up to you.

75
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:12,646
You gonna go back in time or what?

76
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:16,483
[in Korean] I don't have the time
to waste on you right now, okay?

77
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,277
[in English] Just leave me alone.

78
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,822
You can't fix anything, so leave.

79
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:24,908
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

80
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,451
[in Korean] Fine, just go.

81
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,329
I was just trying to be nice.

82
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:31,414
Fine!

83
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,003
Where the heck am I?

84
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,300
Man… I missed my flight.

85
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:47,973
[in English] Kunam,
close up the shop tonight, will ya?

86
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,349
CHARO ISLAND'S ONLY
ASAHI STORE

87
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:51,184
-Yes, sir.
-Mmm.

88
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:58,608
-Mari, would you like to go for a walk?
-[door closes]

89
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:02,904
Let's go for a walk.

90
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:06,032
-Let's walk a little.
-Why are you being weird?

91
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,746
Wanna go for… a walk?

92
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:12,831
I'll pass.

93
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:15,083
-I'm honestly a little wiped out.
-You're tired?

94
00:06:16,543 --> 00:06:18,962
I know an energy drink
that will wake you up instantly.

95
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:23,842
-I'll let you take that.
-Oh.

96
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:25,010
Mari…

97
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,303
Wait a sec.

98
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,560
<i>Come to the village office.</i>

99
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:34,811
Why should I?

100
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:37,188
<i>I'll pay you.</i>

101
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,654
A LEISURELY ISLAND LIFE
RESIDENTS WELCOME!

102
00:06:50,869 --> 00:06:51,870
Huh?

103
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:54,623
I'm not some weirdo.

104
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,834
See, the thing is, I'm actually…

105
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:01,671
So, you see…
I am a properly vetted individual.

106
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:04,132
Let me show you. Here, take a look.

107
00:07:04,215 --> 00:07:05,216
LEE YUBIN - SPATIAL DESIGNER

108
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,926
You can search me up. Yeah, you see that?

109
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:08,219
That's who I am.

110
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:10,138
Got it? Here, look.

111
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:11,931
INVESTORS RAISE OBJECTION

112
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:13,350
Says your company went bust.

113
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:16,311
Exactly, so please buy me dinner.

114
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:17,604
Me?

115
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:19,939
I'll pay you back in one go.

116
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:26,321
Double.

117
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:47,967
What is this place?

118
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:50,762
NOW OFFERING
FATEFUL CURRY OF LOVE

119
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:54,057
[in English] Mari's
"Fateful Curry of Love,"

120
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,392
made from the heart.

121
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:58,687
-Please enjoy!
-Thank you very much.

122
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,271
-Mm-hmm.
-Uh…

123
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,024
[in Korean] Okay, so…

124
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:04,818
What did she say?

125
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,403
She said shut up and eat.

126
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,827
Ah…

127
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,332
[in English] Hey, who's this charming guy?

128
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,460
"Charming guy"? Oh. Who, me?

129
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,260
-It's great. [chuckles]
-It's… It's great?

130
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:31,553
-It's great. Mmm.
-[laughs] It's great.

131
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,805
-Thank you very much.
-Okay, okay, that's enough.

132
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:36,599
Ugh, stop it. Where are we going?

133
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:39,352
-You said you're tired.
-No. Hang on a second, I'm fine now.

134
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:41,438
-Hey. No, wait.
-Bye-bye.

135
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:55,994
[in Korean] If you're done eating,
pay up and go.

136
00:08:58,163 --> 00:08:59,414
Come on, Kunam.

137
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:02,500
I'm not even halfway done.
Don't be so heartless, will you?

138
00:09:02,584 --> 00:09:03,626
Have a seat real quick.

139
00:09:11,426 --> 00:09:12,677
Okay, so…

140
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,597
Tell me, Kunam.

141
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,681
How old are you?

142
00:09:17,599 --> 00:09:19,059
-I'm 27.
-Mmm.

143
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:21,478
Sounds about right.
I'm older, so I'll drop the formalities.

144
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:22,604
I'd rather you didn't.

145
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:25,857
Hey, Kunam, I know it's been tough
for you, all alone in a foreign country.

146
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,150
Well, you must be lonely.

147
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,194
-No, I'm not.
-Of course you are.

148
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:31,738
But not tonight. Not with me here for you.

149
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:33,448
Where should we go?

150
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:35,158
"We"?

151
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,119
Let me crash at yours just for one night.

152
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,623
Just for the night, please.

153
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,383
"One lousy strawberry," he said…

154
00:09:55,804 --> 00:09:59,224
Does he even know how many years
I've poured into each strawberry?

155
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:11,903
-[sighs]
-[chiming stops]

156
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,240
[in Korean] See you never.

157
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:11,504
KARIN'S DAILY CHART

158
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:52,253
-[in English] All right, all right.
-[beeping stops]

159
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:42,720
It's impossible.
There's no way I can do this alone.

160
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:31,185
How do I do this?

161
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,239
[person] Karin.

162
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:45,700
Karin.

163
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,789
Isn't it past your bedtime?

164
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:52,874
Go to bed.

165
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:56,878
Grandpa…

166
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,381
[sighs] There isn't enough time as it is.

167
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:02,133
I shouldn't be wasting it sleeping.

168
00:14:04,052 --> 00:14:07,764
It seems like I've caused you
so much trouble. I'm sorry.

169
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:10,433
It's too much, isn't it?

170
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,935
I won't blame you if you want to give up.

171
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,979
Grandpa, I'm not giving up on this.

172
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:17,607
Not when this farm is your dream.

173
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:19,609
No way.

174
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:24,906
Look how you've grown.

175
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,116
What a sweet girl you are.

176
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,243
Sweeter than a strawberry.

177
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:32,789
I'm failing.

178
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,584
Karin.

179
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,420
Don't worry so much.

180
00:14:39,504 --> 00:14:42,298
The path you've been on is the right one.

181
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:52,683
[Karin] Grandpa…

182
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,743
[teacher] Excuse me!

183
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:12,829
Sorry to bother you.

184
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:26,467
We are so incredibly sorry
for all the trouble we've caused you.

185
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,888
I promise
we'll make up for what we've done,

186
00:15:30,972 --> 00:15:33,015
and we hope that you can forgive us.

187
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:36,727
[children] We're really sorry!

188
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:43,025
Your strawberries were
the best that I ever had.

189
00:15:43,109 --> 00:15:46,696
Yeah, the strawberries on your farm
are number one.

190
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:50,867
This might be overstepping,
but I just wanted to let you know

191
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:53,828
that the children had
the time of their lives that day.

192
00:15:59,542 --> 00:16:01,711
THANK YOU
FOR THE DELICIOUS STRAWBERRIES

193
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:06,132
I want more strawberries!

194
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,425
-Yeah! Me too!
-Me three!

195
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,343
-More! I want more strawberries!
-I want more!

196
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:10,928
-Please, lady.
-Please, Miss.

197
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:13,181
-Please!
-Please, I wanna come back!

198
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:15,474
-Please, please!
-I want more of your strawberries!

199
00:16:20,605 --> 00:16:21,898
Thank you all. [chuckles]

200
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:24,901
I promise
you'll get more strawberries later.

201
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:27,486
[children] Yay! Thank you!

202
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,991
[child] I want more strawberries!

203
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:34,702
[children] Yay! Thank you!

204
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:36,954
I feel like it's going to sell fine.

205
00:16:37,038 --> 00:16:38,706
But then again, maybe it won't.

206
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:41,083
Man, I really hope it sells…

207
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:42,793
This land…

208
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:45,630
Man, it's not going to sell, is it?
How am I going to sell this land?

209
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:46,714
I'll just…

210
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:48,549
No, I have to sell it no matter what.

211
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:49,800
Man, but how?

212
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:53,012
Would you just sit down and wait?
You're getting on my nerves!

213
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,514
Well, I seriously have to sell this land!
I have to, no matter what!

214
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:57,558
I'll sell it off to get back on my feet!

215
00:16:57,642 --> 00:17:00,228
Hyejin. Can't you feel it? Don't you see?

216
00:17:00,311 --> 00:17:02,688
The entire world's waiting
for my comeback.

217
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:04,106
I genuinely don't see it.

218
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,150
-You don't?
-No.

219
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:08,569
-Now sit.
-No, I…

220
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:10,905
Huh? Hey, talk to me, Sanggi.
How did it go?

221
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:12,114
-Hey.
-Did it sell?

222
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:15,201
-Well? Did it?
-Huh? No. It didn't.

223
00:17:19,247 --> 00:17:22,291
Yeah, of course it didn't. I knew it.

224
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:23,626
-I mean, yeah…
-No, wait…

225
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:24,835
I knew he wouldn't buy.

226
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:27,505
Did you see the look on his face?
I knew he wouldn't buy it.

227
00:17:28,005 --> 00:17:29,715
-I had the worst dream last night.
-Hey…

228
00:17:29,799 --> 00:17:32,093
-Gosh, it was so unsettling, you know…
-Yubin.

229
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,553
Look at this, okay?

230
00:17:33,636 --> 00:17:38,015
You know that plot of land
that belongs to that Karin person?

231
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:40,393
Yeah? This bit right here
is the sweet spot.

232
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:42,270
This plot right here leads to the piers.

233
00:17:42,353 --> 00:17:45,773
You have to secure this lot
to make your land worth it.

234
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:48,818
-Yeah?
-Tell me something I don't know.

235
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:50,987
Hey, so listen, yeah?

236
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,406
How about you just buy it yourself?

237
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:57,201
You can pay it off
when you sell your land anyway.

238
00:17:57,285 --> 00:17:59,704
If I were you, I'd buy it in a heartbeat.

239
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,956
This right here. Yeah.

240
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,086
-I've got to go.
-Oh, gosh.

241
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,921
Geez, where are you off to now?

242
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:10,006
Charo Island.

243
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,132
[Hyejin] To do what exactly?

244
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,925
Well, I have to secure that land somehow!

245
00:18:13,009 --> 00:18:14,802
I have to coax that girl
into selling it off.

246
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:16,637
That's the only way
I can get back on my feet.

247
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:18,514
I'll just slide right in, and…

248
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:20,391
-Hey, Yubin. Get a grip.
-I'll be real smooth…

249
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,351
Didn't you say you got
into a big fight with her?

250
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:28,024
Look, people fight.
That's how you get close and build a bond.

251
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:29,817
-That's true. Yeah.
-Okay, Sanggi, Hyejin.

252
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,569
I'll be right back with the land.
Just wait.

253
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:34,572
-Hey, Lee Yubin. Lee Yubin?
-Go get 'em!

254
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:36,949
-[Hyejin] Hey, stop enabling him.
-[Sanggi] Wow, he's fast.

255
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:38,034
TAX ACCOUNTANT CHOI HYEJIN

256
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,423
-[tap opens]
-[water spraying]

257
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:56,594
[Kunam, in English] Mari.

258
00:18:58,304 --> 00:19:00,306
Mari, hang on!

259
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:02,224
Oh, no. Help me.

260
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,309
I'll handle it.

261
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:04,602
[Mari whimpers] Kunam!

262
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:07,146
-Whoa!
-[screams] Kunam, you're making it worse!

263
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:08,564
-Hey, wait!
-[Kunam] Oh, no!

264
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:11,192
-[Karin] You're flooding my whole field!
-[Mari] Kunam.

265
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:12,777
Turn off the water supply, Kunam.

266
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,321
-Over there!
-[in Korean] Oh, right… The water!

267
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:19,450
-[Mari, screaming] What do I do?
-[Kunam] Oh, no, how do I turn this off?

268
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,285
[in English] This is a disaster.

269
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:23,954
-[phone buzzing]
-[sighs]

270
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:27,208
[grunts] Karin speaking.

271
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,335
Yes?

272
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:31,671
Someone is interested? [gasps]

273
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:33,339
Interested in what?

274
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:36,175
-In working here!
-[Mari, Kunam cheering]

275
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:38,010
[Karin] Thank you so much!

276
00:19:38,094 --> 00:19:41,347
-[Mari] I'm so over this hard labor!
-Great. Yes.

277
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,391
[chuckling] Yes!

278
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:45,559
WELCOME TO ODAIRA DISTRICT

279
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:48,521
No matter what you do,
don't overwork this one.

280
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,564
Don't let him even think of running away.

281
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:52,775
I swear that I'll be nicer to this one.

282
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:53,901
-Trust me, okay?
-Mm-hmm.

283
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,988
-[gasps] There he is! Here he comes!
-[squeals]

284
00:19:58,072 --> 00:20:00,866
-[Mari] He's here! [gasps]
-[squeals, chuckles]

285
00:20:31,397 --> 00:20:33,065
What? Huh?

286
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,326
[in Korean] What is it that she needs?

287
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:09,393
A man.

288
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:12,313
A man?

289
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,277
I knew it. See? When I first saw her,

290
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,071
she was having this weird conversation
with that foreign dude. I swear.

291
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:23,282
-That's not what I meant.
-Then what?

292
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,910
What Karin needs is a <i>sagyou-in.</i>

293
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,204
What's a <i>sagyou-in?</i>

294
00:21:28,788 --> 00:21:30,956
A strapping male laborer.

295
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,834
What? A male laborer?

296
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,090
[in English] You're the new field worker?

297
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:42,176
Mm-hmm. Field worker.

298
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:44,136
Is this some kind of joke?

299
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:49,725
As your new field hand,
I'll do whatever you need.

300
00:21:50,226 --> 00:21:52,353
[sighs] I'd rather do
all of this work on my own.

301
00:21:53,646 --> 00:21:55,731
Karin, you can't do this alone.

302
00:21:55,815 --> 00:21:57,566
-Yeah, I know but--
-Dig potatoes,

303
00:21:57,650 --> 00:22:01,028
grow strawberries, dig carrots,
pack them, send them out…

304
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:03,989
[gasps] Are you planning
to force me and Kunam to do it?

305
00:22:04,073 --> 00:22:05,449
But it's this guy.

306
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,370
He's your only option.

307
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:12,540
He doesn't look
like he's touched dirt in his entire life.

308
00:22:12,623 --> 00:22:14,375
Beggars can't be choosers.

309
00:22:15,835 --> 00:22:17,711
I think he'll be good enough.

310
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:21,590
I'll give it all I've got.

311
00:22:23,509 --> 00:22:24,802
Let's do this.

312
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,806
I have a bad feeling about this.

313
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:35,271
How much further up
does this trail even go?

314
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,690
-Whatever, it's nothing.
-[animals howling]

315
00:22:37,773 --> 00:22:39,900
What is this place?
It's like it's haunted or something.

316
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:41,569
Oh.

317
00:22:41,652 --> 00:22:43,737
Hey, wait up!

318
00:22:50,244 --> 00:22:52,079
[in English] This is where you're staying.

319
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,506
THIS IS YOUR LODGING.

320
00:23:05,134 --> 00:23:07,219
Or you can leave if you hate it.

321
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:16,228
[in Korean] No, I just…

322
00:23:16,312 --> 00:23:18,063
Actually, I just wanted to

323
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:23,569
take in the whole place from a distance.

324
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,988
I love the look of this place. It's…

325
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:27,740
very vintage.

326
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,742
[in English] Don't be late tomorrow.

327
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:33,287
Bright and early, Boss.

328
00:23:33,871 --> 00:23:35,456
He won't last one night.

329
00:23:41,462 --> 00:23:43,005
[in Korean] Oh, man.

330
00:23:45,925 --> 00:23:49,136
I'm very picky when it comes
to where I sleep, though. Geez.

331
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:07,488
[in English] Rise and shine.

332
00:24:08,364 --> 00:24:09,823
[in Korean] What the…

333
00:24:09,907 --> 00:24:11,283
[in English] Hear what I said?

334
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:14,286
[in Korean] It's six…

335
00:24:14,787 --> 00:24:16,288
It's six o'clock.

336
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:18,457
[in English] Stop being lazy.

337
00:24:21,794 --> 00:24:24,088
-[groans]
-No sleeping.

338
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:25,172
Get up!

339
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,216
[groans] Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

340
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,342
I'm awake.

341
00:24:41,105 --> 00:24:42,106
Test 1.

342
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,234
Show me how you till soil. Come on.

343
00:24:45,859 --> 00:24:47,778
-Test 1?
-Test 1.

344
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:48,862
Okay.

345
00:24:50,739 --> 00:24:52,157
[in Korean] You want to test me, huh?

346
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:54,785
I've done on-site work for years.

347
00:24:56,662 --> 00:24:58,580
Guess a field this big would take about…

348
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:00,958
Well…

349
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,126
Fifteen minutes?

350
00:25:05,087 --> 00:25:06,547
All right. [grunting]

351
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:16,390
Oh, man!

352
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:26,066
[in English] I asked you to till the soil,
not completely destroy it.

353
00:25:32,031 --> 00:25:33,991
[Karin] You know what a weed is, right?

354
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:43,959
[in Korean] Aha!
Got myself a big one. [chuckles]

355
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:46,879
[in English] That's not a weed.
That is a sweet potato.

356
00:25:51,175 --> 00:25:53,635
You need
to pick the bugs off of the leaves.

357
00:25:53,719 --> 00:25:55,095
-Huh?
-[scoffs]

358
00:25:55,179 --> 00:25:59,183
I said, "You need to get the bugs."

359
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:00,768
-Look. The bugs.
-Huh? What?

360
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:02,352
-Oh. Bugs.
-Right.

361
00:26:02,436 --> 00:26:06,023
-With your hands, pick up the bugs.
-Pick?

362
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:07,232
-Pick.
-Right. Pick.

363
00:26:09,193 --> 00:26:10,736
[in Korean] Where are these bugs?

364
00:26:11,612 --> 00:26:15,157
I don't see any. Oh. [grunts]

365
00:26:19,161 --> 00:26:22,915
-[screaming] Man. A bug!
-[gasps]

366
00:26:23,624 --> 00:26:27,753
A bug! Ew!

367
00:26:32,216 --> 00:26:33,717
Listen, you know that girl, Karin?

368
00:26:33,801 --> 00:26:36,428
Carl? Whatever her name is,
I'm telling you, she's totally crazy.

369
00:26:36,512 --> 00:26:38,722
Huh? Hey, will you listen to me
for a second?

370
00:26:38,806 --> 00:26:42,267
I mean, I know I'm here to work for her,
but she made me sleep in the shed!

371
00:26:42,351 --> 00:26:44,645
I haven't had a single good night's sleep
since I got here.

372
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:46,897
She just throws me
a few steamed sweet potatoes, and then…

373
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:49,775
Listen! Then she worked me like a dog
from 6 a.m. in the morning until now!

374
00:26:49,858 --> 00:26:51,819
Did you think farm work
would be a walk in the park?

375
00:26:51,902 --> 00:26:55,447
I know it's not a walk in the park!
But she's just way over the line! Geez.

376
00:26:55,531 --> 00:26:56,949
And you know what else?

377
00:26:57,741 --> 00:26:59,576
I think she's taking something.

378
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:02,996
She must be hoarding
all the good stuff for herself.

379
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:04,957
She's so tiny, but her stamina is crazy.

380
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,376
See, there's a reason behind that.

381
00:27:08,377 --> 00:27:09,670
What is it?

382
00:27:10,963 --> 00:27:12,965
Karin is actually a bit unwell.

383
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:16,260
That's why everyone here
looks out for her.

384
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:21,265
Is that what it is?

385
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:24,142
Hang in there, man.
Nothing comes easy in life.

386
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:29,439
What's this?

387
00:27:29,523 --> 00:27:31,024
A Japanese textbook?

388
00:27:31,108 --> 00:27:32,651
NEW JAPANESE FOR TOTAL BEGINNERS

389
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,778
This is what got me where I am right now.

390
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:37,239
Doesn't really seem
like a great place to be.

391
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:41,034
Come on, man.
You said you had to get on her good side.

392
00:27:41,118 --> 00:27:44,121
Then, you must be able to talk to her.
You can't use a translator app forever.

393
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:47,124
I should probably study
some Japanese, right?

394
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:50,878
"Excuse me. Where are you going?"

395
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:52,462
[in Korean] That'll be 30,000 won.

396
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,928
[in English] "What is today's date?"

397
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:01,763
[in Korean] Come on, man.
Please buy one off me.

398
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:04,600
It's used. Give me a little discount.

399
00:28:05,309 --> 00:28:07,394
[in English] "It's good to meet you."

400
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:11,148
"It's a pleasure to meet you as well."

401
00:28:11,648 --> 00:28:12,858
[in Korean] What's this?

402
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,403
Huh?

403
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:21,199
Wait, seriously? More sweet potatoes?

404
00:28:22,993 --> 00:28:23,994
What's this?

405
00:28:24,077 --> 00:28:26,413
YASUMI PASS-A
HIGH ABSORPTION MENTHOL COMPOUND

406
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:33,170
Does she think she can…

407
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:37,549
win me over that easily?

408
00:28:49,811 --> 00:28:51,605
THAT'S NOT A NOTEBOOK.

409
00:29:01,365 --> 00:29:04,284
[in English] One, two, three, four.

410
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:08,038
SHIRAHAMA

411
00:29:09,331 --> 00:29:11,375
Ah. Hi there. Good morning.

412
00:29:12,167 --> 00:29:13,168
Morning.

413
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:17,464
Well, um… hmm…

414
00:29:17,965 --> 00:29:20,092
So, uh…

415
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:21,718
Hmm.

416
00:29:22,302 --> 00:29:24,012
[in Korean] Man, I forgot.

417
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:26,682
Where should we start today?

418
00:29:27,683 --> 00:29:28,684
[in English] Ah.

419
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,104
Start with the fertilizer…

420
00:29:35,232 --> 00:29:38,110
No. Focus on the weeding today.

421
00:29:38,193 --> 00:29:40,862
Don't pull out anything
you're not sure of. Got it?

422
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:44,783
[in Korean] Wait, what?
I thought we were working together today.

423
00:29:45,993 --> 00:29:47,828
I have an errand to run.

424
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:49,246
[in Korean] Huh? What…

425
00:29:57,838 --> 00:29:59,673
[in English] I have to do something.

426
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,013
[in Korean] Huh, what…

427
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:18,233
If only…

428
00:30:21,653 --> 00:30:24,072
I could have this little lot.

429
00:30:27,409 --> 00:30:29,619
But why was she in such a bad mood?

430
00:30:31,747 --> 00:30:34,291
Could it be because of this field?

431
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:38,253
Wait, why are they all wilting like this?

432
00:30:41,506 --> 00:30:42,799
Wait a minute.

433
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:49,473
WHEN STRAWBERRY PLANTS WILT

434
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:50,557
REMOVE THE WEAKER PLANTS,

435
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,100
CONTROL THE IRRIGATION,
AND IMPROVE SOIL.

436
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:53,685
SEASHELL FERTILIZER HELPS
YIELD FIRMER STRAWBERRIES!

437
00:30:53,769 --> 00:30:55,020
"Calcium."

438
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:57,397
"Strawberry fertilizer."

439
00:30:57,481 --> 00:31:00,233
FERTILIZER EFFECTIVE
FOR GROWING STRAWBERRIES

440
00:31:00,317 --> 00:31:01,318
Uh-huh.

441
00:31:01,401 --> 00:31:04,821
CALCIUM IN SHELL FERTILIZER
IMPROVES QUALITY AND YIELD

442
00:31:04,905 --> 00:31:05,947
Okay.

443
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:08,950
Let's give it a go.

444
00:31:17,209 --> 00:31:20,170
[grunts] Oh, there it is.

445
00:31:21,630 --> 00:31:22,631
Ugh, my legs.

446
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:28,970
NO ILLEGAL FISHING
FUNAURA FISHING UNION

447
00:31:29,054 --> 00:31:30,263
Now…

448
00:31:31,807 --> 00:31:34,017
Wow, okay.

449
00:31:34,643 --> 00:31:36,269
This should be enough, right?

450
00:31:38,146 --> 00:31:39,564
My foot keeps getting stuck. Geez.

451
00:31:44,194 --> 00:31:45,946
[in English] What are you doing here?

452
00:31:47,322 --> 00:31:49,116
[in Korean] Hey, how'd you know
I was here?

453
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:51,952
Boss! Look at this!

454
00:31:52,035 --> 00:31:55,038
-Look, I caught all of these.
-[in English] Why are you out here

455
00:31:55,122 --> 00:31:57,582
gathering seashells
and not doing the weeding?

456
00:31:58,375 --> 00:32:00,085
-Huh?
-[sighs]

457
00:32:00,710 --> 00:32:02,879
You're not allowed to do this here.

458
00:32:02,963 --> 00:32:04,798
-Come on. Let's…
-[whistle blowing]

459
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:08,885
-Hey! This is a legally protected area!
-We need to run!

460
00:32:08,969 --> 00:32:10,220
-Ready? Run!
-[in Korean] What?

461
00:32:10,303 --> 00:32:11,555
-[stammers]
-[in English] Run! Run!

462
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:13,598
I'm stuck! I can't move!

463
00:32:18,979 --> 00:32:20,272
[in English] Get unstuck!

464
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:48,592
[in Korean] Well, how was I supposed
to know this was illegal?

465
00:32:52,095 --> 00:32:54,848
[in English] Who told you
to come out here and find shells?

466
00:32:58,727 --> 00:33:01,271
[in Korean] I mean,
you seemed a little troubled.

467
00:33:03,857 --> 00:33:07,152
I thought it might be
because of the strawberries,

468
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:09,279
so I wanted to help out.

469
00:33:18,955 --> 00:33:20,081
So, hey.

470
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:23,460
It's fine if we just take
a few of these back with us, right?

471
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:26,296
[in English] No way.

472
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:30,050
I guess I shouldn't, huh?

473
00:33:37,349 --> 00:33:39,226
Mm-hmm. Okay, okay, okay.

474
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:41,019
This is all of them.

475
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:42,103
[in English] Wow.

476
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:44,814
[in Korean] I was hoping to pocket a few.

477
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:47,025
-There.
-[laughs]

478
00:33:49,903 --> 00:33:50,946
That's it. There's no more.

479
00:33:52,489 --> 00:33:54,324
-[in English] None?
-[grunts] None, none.

480
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:55,617
None, none, none.

481
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:57,202
[in Korean] None left. Mmm.

482
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:12,300
[Karin, in English] I almost fell!

483
00:34:27,274 --> 00:34:28,608
[in Korean] Hey, so…

484
00:34:28,692 --> 00:34:30,277
Right. [grunts]

485
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:34,572
About the strawberries.

486
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:40,870
Don't people usually grow strawberries
in greenhouses?

487
00:34:41,621 --> 00:34:44,374
Growing them in an open field seems
like a lot of unnecessary trial and error.

488
00:34:44,457 --> 00:34:45,792
It seems a bit impractical.

489
00:34:47,669 --> 00:34:49,045
[Karin, in English] You're right.

490
00:34:49,129 --> 00:34:52,382
In a greenhouse,
the environment is controlled.

491
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:55,677
-It would make my life a lot easier.
-[in Korean] Right.

492
00:34:58,138 --> 00:34:59,514
So what if…

493
00:35:01,349 --> 00:35:02,350
And that's a huge "if."

494
00:35:02,434 --> 00:35:04,352
What if someone were to buy
that land for a lot of money?

495
00:35:04,436 --> 00:35:05,979
Wouldn't it make more
sense to just sell it off,

496
00:35:06,062 --> 00:35:08,315
move your crops,
and upgrade to a big greenhouse?

497
00:35:08,398 --> 00:35:09,941
It'd be way more convenient.

498
00:35:13,445 --> 00:35:15,113
[in English] That's true in theory.

499
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:18,074
Fruit grows in rhythm
with every single season,

500
00:35:19,034 --> 00:35:21,286
allowing nature's flavor to absorb.

501
00:35:27,876 --> 00:35:30,253
I learned that from my grandfather.

502
00:35:30,337 --> 00:35:34,382
Which is why I decided to grow
my strawberries outside instead.

503
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:40,221
You could say that
it's a personal experiment.

504
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:43,516
Does it really make a difference or not?

505
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:47,520
Does the power of mother nature
affect how delicious they can be?

506
00:35:53,193 --> 00:35:55,987
Anyway, I noticed your effort today.

507
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:58,239
Although you were barely any help.

508
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:01,743
Is that a compliment or an insult?

509
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:06,247
[in English] In appreciation,
you can come over for dinner.

510
00:36:06,956 --> 00:36:07,999
You earned it.

511
00:36:17,092 --> 00:36:18,218
[in Korean] Let's go!

512
00:36:46,788 --> 00:36:47,789
Good evening.

513
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:49,833
Ah.

514
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:53,002
Hi. Good evening. Have a seat.

515
00:36:54,129 --> 00:36:55,130
Ah.

516
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:56,631
-Ah.
-[Karin] Mmm.

517
00:36:56,715 --> 00:36:58,925
[chuckles] Please, wait a minute.

518
00:37:19,028 --> 00:37:20,405
CERTIFICATE OF RECOGNITION

519
00:37:30,206 --> 00:37:31,207
[in Korean] Huh?

520
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:33,793
Wow.

521
00:37:34,711 --> 00:37:37,005
This guy's from my favorite game
when I was little.

522
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:38,423
What are the chances?

523
00:37:40,967 --> 00:37:41,968
[in English] Okay.

524
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:44,929
Come sit. It's ready.

525
00:37:45,013 --> 00:37:46,181
Ah.

526
00:37:49,017 --> 00:37:50,018
Here you are.

527
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:53,646
Okay.

528
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:59,444
I know when it's better to use
the carrot or the stick.

529
00:38:06,034 --> 00:38:08,870
What are you going to make me do tomorrow?

530
00:38:11,164 --> 00:38:12,707
-[in English] You're not hungry?
-[in Korean] No, no.

531
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:15,001
[in English] Uh. Thank you for the meal.

532
00:38:16,127 --> 00:38:17,462
Time to eat.

533
00:38:19,547 --> 00:38:21,382
Oh! I forgot something.

534
00:38:21,466 --> 00:38:22,675
Huh?

535
00:38:27,514 --> 00:38:29,557
You should know what this is.

536
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,852
Korean-style pickled perilla leaves.

537
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:35,480
Oh?

538
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:38,149
[in Korean] Wait, this is a Korean
side dish. How do you know it?

539
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:42,862
[in English] When I was little,
a Korean man used to board with us.

540
00:38:42,946 --> 00:38:44,531
I learned the recipe from him.

541
00:38:45,615 --> 00:38:46,616
Oh.

542
00:38:47,242 --> 00:38:52,622
The red pepper is for "love,"
and the daikon radish is for "health."

543
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:59,045
So you're getting both love and health.

544
00:39:08,471 --> 00:39:09,556
[in Korean] There.

545
00:39:10,265 --> 00:39:11,266
Hmm?

546
00:39:11,850 --> 00:39:14,102
This again? I'm so sick of it.

547
00:39:14,769 --> 00:39:16,688
It's your dad's favorite.

548
00:39:16,771 --> 00:39:19,148
He hasn't been home in a while,
so stop complaining and eat.

549
00:39:19,232 --> 00:39:23,111
Son, this dish here
is full of love and health.

550
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:24,612
Take a look.

551
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,656
Here's love.

552
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:29,450
And here's health.

553
00:39:31,035 --> 00:39:32,537
<i>And you wrap it up…</i>

554
00:39:35,832 --> 00:39:37,083
Just try it.

555
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:40,920
-For you.
-Me? [chuckles]

556
00:39:41,004 --> 00:39:42,463
Your health matters the most.

557
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:44,549
I can't say no to that.

558
00:39:48,761 --> 00:39:50,972
That man was so kind to us.

559
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:55,018
He took extra care of my grandpa
after he collapsed.

560
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:58,479
And he taught me
a lot about growing strawberries.

561
00:40:00,982 --> 00:40:05,987
Mr. Gyeongsu was a very wonderful man,
but you're the complete opposite.

562
00:40:09,991 --> 00:40:11,159
Ah…

563
00:40:12,702 --> 00:40:15,163
I'm actually not feeling so great. Sorry.

564
00:40:42,732 --> 00:40:44,651
What on earth was he doing here?

565
00:40:45,401 --> 00:40:47,362
INTERNAL USE

566
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:36,411
-[panting echoing]
-[high-pitched ringing]

567
00:41:37,787 --> 00:41:38,788
[Yubin] <i>Mom.</i>

568
00:42:00,643 --> 00:42:01,644
[sobbing] Mom.

569
00:42:02,812 --> 00:42:04,480
Mom!

570
00:43:29,398 --> 00:43:31,192
[in Korean] Are you okay?

571
00:44:09,605 --> 00:44:11,858
MERRY BERRY LOVE

572
00:44:11,941 --> 00:44:13,025
NEXT EPISODE

573
00:44:13,109 --> 00:44:15,695
[Karin, in English] <i>We are not sleeping</i>
<i>in the same space.</i>

574
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:17,905
[Yubin] <i>I love rules. I really do.</i>

575
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:20,158
-[in Korean] Rock, paper, scissors!
-[both scream]

576
00:44:20,241 --> 00:44:21,909
<i>Why is my heart pounding?</i>
